Comparison: LangChain + LangGraph vs Custom Python

AI Supply Chain Intelligence – Delay Detection & Solution BOT, 
cbuild everything with plain Python. 
The main reason to use LangChain + LangGraph is that they provide reusable building blocks and workflow management, 
reducing the amount of infrastructure code you need to write and maintain.

========

| Feature               | LangChain + LangGraph           | Custom Python                 |
| --------------------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| Development Speed     | ✅ Faster                        | ❌ Slower                      |
| Code Size             | ✅ Less code                     | ❌ More code                   |
| Workflow Management   | ✅ Built-in graph                | ❌ Manual function calls       |
| State Management      | ✅ Built-in state                | ❌ Manual dictionaries/classes |
| Tool Integration      | ✅ Standard tool interface       | ❌ Write your own              |
| Prompt Management     | ✅ Prompt templates              | ❌ Manual string formatting    |
| Memory                | ✅ Built-in memory options       | ❌ Implement yourself          |
| RAG Integration       | ✅ Ready-made components         | ❌ Build from scratch          |
| Vector DB Integration | ✅ Simple wrappers               | ❌ Direct API handling         |
| LLM Integration       | ✅ One interface for many models | ❌ Separate code per provider  |
| Multi-Agent Support   | ✅ Native workflows              | ❌ Complex custom logic        |
| Debugging             | ✅ LangSmith support             | ❌ Manual logging              |
| Scalability           | ✅ Easy to extend                | ❌ Refactoring often needed    |
| Learning Curve        | ⚠️ Moderate                      | ✅ Easy (know Python)          |
| External Dependency   | ❌ Depends on libraries          | ✅ Pure Python                 |
